l":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":351,"closed_issues":2337,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T15:17:38Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":17,"created_at":"2025-10-16T03:04:15Z","updated_at":"2026-06-22T13:34:57Z","closed_at":"2026-06-22T13:34:30Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.5.1\nVSCode godot-tools extension v2.5.1\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 24H2 (26100.6584)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIt's hard for me to be helpful in describing this issue because I genuinely just have no idea what's going on. My issue seems to be directly caused by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104401, which, ironically, aimed to fix this. \nI am getting the seemingly ages-old \"Class [x] hides a global script class\" error and a warning that \"The language server might not work correctly if the project opened in Godot isn't the same\" after upgrading from Godot 4.4.1 to Godot 4.5.1.\n\nI have tried everything I could think of, my VSC workspace is a multi-root workspace (but only has one godot project) and so while it was working fine in Godot 4.4, I did try having Godot open VSC directly with the project folder but the issue still occurs. \nMy project filepath isn't particularly weird, for reference: `F:\\Programming_Projects\\MaidManager\\MaidManager` \n(yes, duplicate names, the top-level being the workspace with other folders, and the nested one being the Godot project folder) (not that it matters since the issue happens regardless of whether it's the top-level or nested folder that is opened in VSC)\n\nPS: I wasn't sure whether this issue should have been opened in the godot-vscode-plugin repo or here, but I chose here since, as far as I could tell, this issue is directly caused by PR 104401 in this repo\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nThe MRP was created under the following path:  `F:\\Programming_Projects\\lsp-path-matching-mrp`\n1) Open the project in Godot 4.5.1\n2) Open VSC with godot-tools v2.5.1(or any other tool that connects to the language server) \n3) If my environment isn't uniquely cursed, you should get a mismatched workspaces warning and the \"Class [x] hides a global script\" error when opening the test .gdscript\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[lsp-path-matching-mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22939503/lsp-path-matching-mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111702/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"e